      {
        "id": "notes",
        "position": [
          2,
          1
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "**SP08 \u2014 Where did the tone amplitude go?**  \n**Does the tallest FFT bin equal the amplitude of an off-bin tone?**  \nRun 2 s at 128 Hz. Analyze 0\u20131 s: N=128, \u0394f=1 Hz; a 16.5 Hz tone leaks. Analyze 0\u20132 s: N=256, \u0394f=0.5 Hz; it is coherent.  \nUse Rectangular, Peak amplitude, Linear, All inputs, Remove mean off. Edit test frequency_hz 16.5 \u2192 18; predict a single-bin peak.  \n[Open SP08 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/SP08-dft-leakage/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT teaching materials](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_lec18/) \u00b7 [S7 spectrum guide](qrc:/s7studio/help/docs/STUDIO_SPECTRUM.md)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1298,
          "height": 340,
          "font_size": 18
        }
      }
    ]
  }
